(vector 
 (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "2607182400")
  (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-lei-update-routine: automated hourly LEI collection via murakumo + itonami-actor")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/decided "2026-07-18")
  (:adr/body "## Summary

Formalize LEI collection as a scheduled cloud routine on murakumo.cloud:
- **Frequency**: Hourly (or daily, TBD by ops)
- **Pattern**: cloud-itonami actor (Advisor⊣Governor) orchestrates bin/collect.bb
- **Integration**: GLEIF API + ToS fetch + LEI repo scaffold + progress.edn ledger
- **Output**: cloud-itonami-lei-* repos pushed to GitHub + IPNS graph updated

## Design

### 1. Fleet Registration (manifest/fleet-db.edn)

Register new cell entry:
```edn
{:cell/id \"itonami-lei-update-hourly\"
 :cell/type :cloud-routine
 :cell/actor \"cloud-itonami-isic-8291\"
 :cell/frequency \"0 * * * *\" ;; hourly
 :cell/entrypoint \"bin/collect.bb\"
 :cell/args \"--scope all\"
 :cell/environment {:SUPERPROJECT_ROOT \".\"
                    :MURAKUMO_CELL \"itonami-lei-update-hourly\"}
 :cell/lease {:ttl 3600 :max-retries 2}
 :cell/governor :enabled}
```

### 2. Cloud Routine Wrapper (bin/collect-routine.clj)

Orchestrator that:
- Reads progress.edn from S3 / git (worktree side-effect isolation)
- Calls `(op/build db {:op :disclosure/discover-candidates ...})`
- Invokes bin/collect.bb for execution
- Captures output → append-only ledger (manifest/fleet-db.ledger.edn)
- Reports: ✅ X repos created, ⚠ Y JS-rendered-SPA failures, ❌ Z network errors

### 3. IPNS Graph Publication

After successful collection:
- Derive isic-8291's CACAO did:key graph
- Publish to IPNS (via murakumo-supplied kotobase-llm cell)
- Write root hash to kotobase.net discovery surface

### 4. Governance Model

- **Proposal**: bin/collect.bb scans progress.edn, generates batch `{:vertical :candidates}`
- **Governor approval**: 6-stage gate (source-basis, scope, licensed-disclosure, relationship, high-stakes, outcome)
- **Commitment**: Batch scaffold + push + ledger append (atomic per batch)
- **Audit trail**: Each collection tick logged in append-only `fleet-db.ledger.edn`

## Scope & Limitations

### Scope
- **New capacity**: Automated discovery for new verticals (if owner declares new scope: COFOG / UNSPSC / etc.)
- **Retry queue**: JS-rendered-SPA failures collected in `retry-js-rendered.edn`; manual chrome-automation separate

### Honest Limitations
- **JS-rendered ToS**: HTTP fetch cannot execute JavaScript. SPA pages fail with 403/empty-body; queued for later.
- **Rate limiting**: GLEIF API throttled; collect.bb respects backoff (hardcoded delay between requests)
- **Idempotency**: LEI repo already exists → skip scaffold, re-verify ToS doc count (no duplicate repos)

## Verification

- **Unit test**: `test/dossier/discover_candidates_integration_test.clj` (existing, validates StateGraph)
- **E2E dry-run**: `bb bin/collect.bb --dry-run --scope=isic` (scaffold generation, no push)
- **Smoke**: Deploy to murakumo with 1-hour lease, monitor first tick for:
  - Proposal generated ✅
  - Governor approved ✅
  - Repos created + pushed ✅
  - Progress ledger appended ✅
  - IPNS graph updated ✅

## Sequence

1. **[Next iteration]** Register `itonami-lei-update-hourly` in fleet-db.edn
2. **[Next iteration]** Write `bin/collect-routine.clj` wrapper (Governor orchestration)
3. **[Next iteration]** Deploy to murakumo cell (test with short TTL first)
4. **[Parallel]** Seed IPNS publish routine via murakumo-supplied kotobase-llm
5. **[Monitor]** Observe 3–5 ticks; log any failures to retry queue

## Related

- **ADR-2607182300** — Part C LEI discovery automation (skeleton → full implementation done)
- **ADR-2607110300** — Progress tracker + methodology (baseline, ISIC/ISCO complete)
- **ADR-2607150100** — Registry lookups are deterministic, NOT governor-gated
- **ADR-2607110400** — Governor 6-stage pipeline (reused here)
- **ADR-2605192200** — Charter Rider (Actor identity, CACAO, transparent force)

## Implementation Notes

- Use existing `bin/collect.bb` as the execution engine (no new script needed)
- Wrapper `bin/collect-routine.clj` handles: progress I/O, error classification, ledger append
- Murakumo cell provides: lease/retry/heartbeat infrastructure + DNS failover
- IPNS publish: route via existing kotobase-llm (ADR-2607110300 D6 forward reference)

## Success Criteria

- ✅ First automated tick completes without human intervention
- ✅ Progress.edn ledger appends with 1 commit per tick (immutable)
- ✅ No repo duplicates on retry/re-run
- ✅ JS-rendered-SPA failures properly classified + queued for retry
- ✅ IPNS graph updated with new isic-8291 did:key + member attestations")
